  "skip_justification": "Skips L8: the cell responds to cytosolic calcium through channel and receptor proteins housed in subcellular structures (sarcoplasmic reticulum, T-tubule), both of which are present in this substrate and traversable. The edge is a compression of that chain, stated at cell level because the cell-level response is what the sources characterise."
 },
 {
  "id": "REL:crossbridge-contributes-heart-function",
  "source": "HOX:mechanism:cross-bridge-cycle",
  "target": "UBERON:0000948",
  "type": "contributes_to",
  "provenance_claim": "CLM:heart-function-pump",
  "compilation_status": "structured",
  "skip_justification": "Skips L8 (sarcomere), L7 (cardiomyocyte), L6 (population), L5 (myocardium) and L4 (ventricle). Admitted as a compression of the full chain, every link of which is present in this substrate and traversable; it is not asserted as a direct mechanism, and the relation type is contributes_to rather than causes."
 },
 {
  "id": "REL:assoc-autonomic-cardiaccycle",
  "source": "HOX:mechanism:cross-bridge-cycle",
  "target": "UBERON:0000948",
  "type": "associated_with",
  "provenance_claim": "CLM:heart-two-pumps-series",
  "compilation_status": "narrative",
  "prose_justification": "Seed corpus cross-link: 'Sympathetic and parasympathetic input continuously fine-tune the heart's own intrinsic pacemaker rate.' The corpus states that a relationship exists; it does not state its type. Typing this requires a curator decision with a source (FR-REL-007).",
  "skip_justification": "The corpus asserts that a relationship exists without stating its type or its intermediate steps. That is precisely why this edge is associated_with rather than regulates: the skipped levels are unknown because the relationship is uncompiled, not because they were judged unnecessary."
 },
